{"title":"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>How many of the following numbers are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fb33abc44e402af942d985c5fe1c52cbc9a0684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99, 64, 57, 26, 30, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b14ef560acadba8244952e9a8d5481f494445dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are all divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can also use the fact that the sum of the digits of the numbers is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all of these numbers. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17ebc4f23fcc9579bcab96f79fdbb942d9985f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 9 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89cf8c8bdac93c00d0c6f3786baab5a3cf3e872f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 8 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, which is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers so far.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more number, meaning that we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Otherwise, we would still have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">player 1</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a2b1091166a6e32e6ddaec65386d3e713011cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we then would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" /> numbers that are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC\">2024 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">Relay B Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Relay B Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" titl